  // currentConstrained segment that is intended to stay inside a << >> arithmetic
  // span. At each step it decides whether to decode freely or with parser-based
  // constraints by checking whether currentConstrained is complete. When outside a
  // constrained span, it uses unconstrained decoding and starts a constrained
  // segment once a token containing "<<" appears. When inside a constrained span,
  // it uses constrained decoding so the arithmetic content remains parser-valid,
  // and it resets the constrained segment after a token containing ">>" appears.
  // This minimal state supports the task by letting normal explanatory text be
  // generated freely while giving verifier-friendly evidence for parser-valid
  // constrained generation within delimiter-marked computations.
  // CSD_RATIONALE_END
